1
00:00:03,210 --> 00:00:05,950
Freeman:自从人类诞生以来，
Freeman: Since the dawn of our species,

2
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:10,280
这个物种就在不断进步。
humanity has never stopped moving forward.

3
00:00:10,290 --> 00:00:13,900
首先，我们学会了使用火，
First, we mastered fire.

4
00:00:13,910 --> 00:00:16,060
[ Explosion ]

5
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:20,760
时至今日，我们探究宇宙的时空结构。
Today, we play with the fabric of space and time.

6
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:24,500
现在，现代技术即将超越
Now technology is about to advance

7
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:27,200
我们最狂野的梦想。
beyond our wildest dreams.

8
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:31,300
我们也许马上就能知晓未来...
We may soon know the future...

9
00:00:31,310 --> 00:00:36,840
并以光速移动。
And learn to move matter at the speed of light.

10
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:41,050
作为凡人的我们，能否凌驾于宇宙之上呢？
Could we mortals ever gain power over the entire universe?

11
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:45,700
我们会成为神吗？
Will we become God?

12
00:00:51,710 --> 00:00:56,560
空间，时间，生命本身。
Space, time, life itself.

13
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:02,800
宇宙的奥秘，尽在穿越虫洞。
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

14
00:01:10,510 --> 00:01:13,810
我们会成为神吗？

15
00:01:15,350 --> 00:01:16,580
[ thunderclap, rain falling ]

16
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:18,420
圣经告诉我们
The Bible says

17
00:01:19,420 --> 00:01:26,160
上帝掌管着天地间的一切，
that God is the master of all things in heaven and on earth,

18
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:31,230
上帝创造了我们，指引着世界的走向。
that God created us and guides the world we live in.

19
00:01:31,230 --> 00:01:33,710
但掌管着整个宇宙的
But a total mastery of the universe

20
00:01:33,730 --> 00:01:37,000
或许并非神灵，
may not be just a divine power.

21
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:39,900
而是命中注定的我们，
It could be our destiny.

22
00:01:39,910 --> 00:01:43,470
我们将来也许不仅扮演神...
Will we someday not only play God...

23
00:01:46,180 --> 00:01:48,580
或许会成为神。
But  be God?

24
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:53,320
我们获得全能之力后，又会做什么呢？
And what will we do with our omnipotence?

25
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:55,820
[ Birds chirping ]

26
00:01:56,820 --> 00:02:00,260
小时候我扮演牛仔，
I played cowboys when I was a kid.

27
00:02:02,530 --> 00:02:05,330
偷袭是我的标志性动作。
The sneak attack was my trademark move.

28
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:07,760
[ Click ]

29
00:02:07,770 --> 00:02:11,800
在我创造的牛仔世界里，子弹无法对我造成伤害，
Freeman: In the world I created, bullets couldn't harm me.

30
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:14,440
我是不可战胜的，
I was invincible.

31
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:18,340
我可以做我想要的一切。
I could do anything I wanted.

32
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:22,610
这样的神力会有一天
Could these God-like powers one day be a reality

33
00:02:22,610 --> 00:02:24,310
出现在真实世界中吗？
in the real world?

34
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:34,520
加州大学伯克利分校的生物工程学家Adam Arkin认为
U.C. Berkeley bioengineer Adam Arkin

35
00:02:34,530 --> 00:02:38,110
我们已经很接近拥有神力了--
believes we are very close to one divine ability --

36
00:02:39,110 --> 00:02:42,130
那就是创造新的生命形式。
creating new forms of life.

37
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:44,030
想要证据？
Want evidence?

38
00:02:44,030 --> 00:02:47,670
他正坐在证据上面。
He's sitting right on top of it.

39
00:02:47,670 --> 00:02:50,870
Arkin：这些看起来像有机体的家具
Arkin: Well, these very organic-looking pieces of furniture

40
00:02:50,870 --> 00:02:53,460
实际上是由一种快速生长的真菌形成的。
are actually formed out of a fast-growing fungus.

41
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:55,680
这是由艺术家Philip Ross创作的，
The artist's name is Philip Ross.

42
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:58,200
他称这类艺术品叫“真菌建筑”(mycotecture)，
【个人原创翻译，若有学术翻译请告知，感谢！】
He calls this type of work mycotecture,

43
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:01,800
因为研究真菌的学科叫真菌学，
because the study of fungi is mycology,

44
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:05,900
这些就是真菌构成的建筑。
and so they're like architecture of fungus.

45
00:03:07,010 --> 00:03:10,360
艺术家们在木头上种植蘑菇，
Freeman: The artist crafted these tools

46
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:13,390
然后就得到了这些家具，
by feeding wood chips to mushrooms.

47
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:17,600
当蘑菇“吃掉”木头后，长出了互相联结的纤维，
As the mushrooms feast, they grow fibers that interlock,

48
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:21,820
形成了比混凝土还坚硬的物质。
forming a substance that is stronger than concrete.

49
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:26,040
我们正在学着如何塑造生命来为我们服务。
We are learning how to shape life to fit our needs.

50
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:29,540
但Adam想要把这种观点更进一步发展，
But Adam wants to take this idea a step further,

51
00:03:29,550 --> 00:03:32,480
造出能够根据我们的打算
to have living objects shape themselves

52
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:34,230
改变自身的活物，
according to our design,

53
00:03:34,230 --> 00:03:40,320
就像圣经里说的，上帝用亚当的肋骨造出了夏娃。
just as the Bible says God shaped Eve from Adam's rib.

54
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,620
我们想要做的
What we would like to do as engineers

55
00:03:42,630 --> 00:03:44,030
就是给细胞编程，
is to program the cells

56
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:46,780
让它们自组装成多种形状，
to self-organize into shapes like this,

57
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:48,760
或成为比这些凳子
or into more complicated, articulated shapes

58
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:50,100
更为复杂连贯的形状。
than even this is.

59
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:53,870
Adam的理想是创造出能够
Freeman: Adam's dream is to create living organisms

60
00:03:53,870 --> 00:03:56,500
感受其周围环境
that can sense their surroundings

61
00:03:56,510 --> 00:03:59,640
并按需改变自身形状的生物。
and change their shape on demand.

62
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:03,480
不仅像蘑菇凳子一样总是凳子，
Instead of a mushroom chair always being a chair,

63
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:06,480
更要它知道Adam疲惫时...
it would know when Adam got tired...

64
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:08,850
然后自发地
Wow. And then, organically,

65
00:04:08,850 --> 00:04:12,620
将自己变成蘑菇床。
morph itself into a mushroom bed.

66
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:14,860
[打哈欠和鼾声]
[ Yawns and snores ]

67
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:16,820
为了完成这样的工作，他需要了解
To do this, he needs to learn

68
00:04:16,830 --> 00:04:19,630
如何控制活细胞中的
how to control the movement of molecules

69
00:04:19,630 --> 00:04:21,460
分子运动。
inside living cells.

70
00:04:21,460 --> 00:04:23,400
[ Continues snoring ]

71
00:04:28,340 --> 00:04:31,570
想象这位舞者
Arkin: Well, imagine the dancer is a molecule

72
00:04:31,570 --> 00:04:33,610
是她细胞内的一个分子，
that's going inside her cell.

73
00:04:34,510 --> 00:04:37,680
分子行为决定了细胞行为，
Molecules are what make the cell act.

74
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:39,080
它们相互作用，
They bounce into each other,

75
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:40,950
互相结合、互相拉扯伸展，
they bind, they pull, they stretch,

76
00:04:40,950 --> 00:04:43,850
这样，才使得细胞
and in doing so, make the cell do, you know,

77
00:04:43,850 --> 00:04:46,090
做出各种行为，
do all these amazing acrobatics,

78
00:04:46,090 --> 00:04:49,050
所有的这些都可以开发，为我们自身服务。
all of which we can exploit for our own needs.

79
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:51,890
每时每刻，细胞行为
Freeman: Every movement a cell makes

80
00:04:51,890 --> 00:04:55,130
都遵循DNA编码的指导，
stems from instructions in its D.N.A. code.

81
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:58,500
Adam微妙的改变了DNA，
Adam had been subtly altering this code

82
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:01,720
按照我们的需要
to change how the molecules in a cell

83
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:04,650
改变了细胞内的分子行为。
are programmed to perform.

84
00:05:04,660 --> 00:05:07,510
作为细胞工程学家，我们要做的就是
As cytoengineers, what we're able to do these days

85
00:05:07,510 --> 00:05:09,480
获取DNA，并将其改编，
is to take D.N.A., engineer it,

86
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:11,960
然后放回细胞中，就能够得到
and put it back inside cells so it can direct

87
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:13,710
你看到的舞者的行为，
the dancer you're seeing here,

88
00:05:13,710 --> 00:05:15,480
我们也能在计算机上
and so we can, on a computer,

89
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:17,620
编码我们希望获得什么样的结果，
program what we expect to see happen,

90
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:20,920
然后写入DNA，放回细胞中，
make that into D.N.A., put it into the cells,

91
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:24,760
然后看细胞是否会表现我们设计的行为。
and then watch to see if they follow our instructions.

92
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:30,500
如果Adam能够控制一个细胞的行为，
If Adam can control the behavior of one cell,

93
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:34,900
想象下使用多个细胞能干出什么，
imagine what he can do with many.

94
00:05:34,900 --> 00:05:39,540
他能将细胞编程，让它们按照他的需要生长，
He could program cells to grow into whatever he wants.

95
00:05:39,540 --> 00:05:42,740
他可以造出一个苹果...
He could create an apple...

96
00:05:42,740 --> 00:05:43,940
一棵树，
a tree,

97
00:05:43,940 --> 00:05:48,050
甚至连上帝都没考虑过的东西，
or maybe something even God never considered,

98
00:05:48,050 --> 00:05:50,080
比如活的自行车。
like a living bicycle.

99
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:53,350
在自行车这个例子中，每部分都要协调工作，
In the case of the bicycle, each part has to work together.

100
00:05:53,350 --> 00:05:55,820
有齿轮、车轮和车把，
There's gears and wheels and steering, and the like.

101
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:59,220
这样每个细胞都要意识到周围环境，
And so, each cell has to be aware of its surrounds

102
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:01,930
与其他细胞共同工作，每个细胞都是不同，
and work with other cells, each one different,

103
00:06:01,930 --> 00:06:03,410
每个细胞都有自己的工作，
each one with its own job.

104
00:06:03,410 --> 00:06:07,100
这也是我们对其进行编程后的结果。
And part of our instruction set is to make that happen.

105
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,730
Adam的工作
Adam's work could be the foundation

106
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:12,040
为创造现代伊甸园奠定了基础，
for creating a modern garden of eden,

107
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:13,870
在这里不是上帝，
where we, not God,

108
00:06:13,870 --> 00:06:18,680
而是我们决定这里存活着何种生物。
get to decide what kind of life grows inside of it.

109
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:24,380
我认为人类想要得到控制世界的感觉，
I think humans want to feel in control over their world.

110
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:28,420
我们这种生物建造东西、
We are animals that build things and control things

111
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:29,820
掌控并改变事物，
and change things, and I think

112
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:32,690
我认为这是我们认识自己的过程。
it's part in process with who we are.

113
00:06:34,190 --> 00:06:36,030
圣经告诉我们，
Freeman: The Bible says,

114
00:06:36,130 --> 00:06:40,430
“上帝的终极作品是创造了
"God's ultimate creations were man and woman --

115
00:06:40,430 --> 00:06:43,470
有自由意志的男人和女人。”
beings with their own free will."

116
00:06:43,470 --> 00:06:46,190
我们已经创造了新的生命形式，
We have already crafted new life-forms,

117
00:06:46,190 --> 00:06:51,510
但我们的作品中是否具有意识灵魂呢？
but could our creations ever have conscious souls?

118
00:06:51,510 --> 00:06:54,210
大多科学家认为意识体验
Most scientists consider conscious experience

119
00:06:54,210 --> 00:06:56,380
是难以捉摸的，
to be an elusive property

120
00:06:56,380 --> 00:06:59,650
也许永远不能被彻底理解，
that may never be fully understood,

121
00:06:59,650 --> 00:07:02,320
更别提人工创造的了。
much less artificially created.

122
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:05,020
但就职于威斯康星大学的
But neuroscientist Melanie Bolling,

123
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:08,090
神经科学家Melanie Bolling
from the University of Wisconsin-Madison,

124
00:07:08,090 --> 00:07:10,630
并不认为意识有那么神秘。
doesn't think it's so mysterious.

125
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:16,730
她认为意识可以归结与一个简单的数字。
In fact, she thinks it can be boiled down to a single number.

126
00:07:16,730 --> 00:07:21,800
我们的工作就是量化意识，
What we try to do in our work is to quantify consciousness.

127
00:07:21,810 --> 00:07:23,090
量化工作中，我们会说
By the quantity, we say,

128
00:07:23,090 --> 00:07:25,010
“理解的量是多少？
"How much understanding there is?

129
00:07:25,010 --> 00:07:26,770
一个系统中有多少意识？”
How much consciousness there is in a system?"

130
00:07:32,570 --> 00:07:34,920
了解意识的一种方法
One way to understand consciousness

131
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:37,520
就是观察意识被破坏时会发生什么。
is to observe what happens when it fails.

132
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:40,060
不同的脑损伤
Different brain injuries

133
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:43,990
有着差异非常显著的结果。
have dramatically different consequences.

134
00:07:43,990 --> 00:07:45,660
我们从神经学中了解到
We learn from neurology

135
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:48,230
有一些脑损伤
that there are some brain lesions

136
00:07:48,230 --> 00:07:51,530
会使你失去意识，而有些不会。
that make you unconscious and some that don't.

137
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:55,600
Freeman:当大脑皮层受到了损伤，
Freeman: When damage occurs in the cerebral cortex,

138
00:07:55,610 --> 00:07:57,910
像心脏或肺这样的器官
body organs like the heart and lungs

139
00:07:57,910 --> 00:07:59,440
还可以继续工作，
may continue to function.

140
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:02,580
但是，病人不会对他周围的环境
However, a patient won't show any awareness

141
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:04,430
产生任何意识。
of his or her environment.

142
00:08:04,430 --> 00:08:05,680
[ Buzzing ]

143
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:09,030
但如果一个人只有小脑受到损伤，
But a person with injuries only to the cerebellum

144
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:11,890
他仍可以完好的保持清醒与警觉。
could still be perfectly awake and alert.

145
00:08:11,890 --> 00:08:15,490
虽然组成小脑的神经元比大脑皮层多，
Even though the cerebellum has many more neurons

146
00:08:15,490 --> 00:08:20,060
但它并不会产生意识。
than the cortex, it doesn't play a vital role in consciousness.

147
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:23,300
当你观察大脑皮层
So when you look at what makes the difference

148
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:26,100
和小脑的差别时，
between the cortex and the cerebellum,

149
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:30,140
你会发现差别并不在神经元的数量上，
you will see that the difference is not in the number of neurons.

150
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:32,360
这种差别则体现在
What is making the difference is

151
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:35,980
不同脑区域之间的交流方式上。
the way the different brain areas talk to each other.

152
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:42,530
我们可以把脑中单个的神经元
Imagine that each neuron throughout the brain

153
00:08:42,530 --> 00:08:44,320
想象成灯泡，
is a light bulb.

154
00:08:46,990 --> 00:08:51,930
如果每个灯泡都有自己的开关会怎样呢？
What would happen if every single one had its own switch?

155
00:08:51,930 --> 00:08:53,560
[ Switch clicks ]

156
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:56,400
如果我把这个灯泡打开，
So if I turn this light on,

157
00:08:56,400 --> 00:09:00,050
它不会对系统里的其他部分产生影响。
it won't make any difference to the rest of the system.

158
00:09:00,050 --> 00:09:01,750
Freeman:Melanie认为
Freeman: Melanie believes

159
00:09:01,750 --> 00:09:04,540
意识源于大脑皮层，
that consciousness arises in the cortex,

160
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:06,870
因为产生意识的神经元
because the neurons it stems from

161
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:09,740
并不像这些独立的灯泡，
are not isolated bulbs.

162
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:14,430
它们形成了相互联系的网络结构。
They form an interconnected network that communicates.

163
00:09:14,430 --> 00:09:18,250
如果我有一些相互联系的灯泡，
If we had a set of lamps that are connected to each other,

164
00:09:18,250 --> 00:09:21,520
打开或关闭某个灯泡
then actually turning the lamp on or off

165
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:25,260
就会对系统的其他部分产生影响，
would make a lot of difference to the rest of the system.

166
00:09:25,260 --> 00:09:26,660
这样我们就认为
And there, we would say

167
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:29,330
它们之间的信息是整合并共享的。
that the information is shared or integrated.

168
00:09:29,330 --> 00:09:31,980
Freeman：现在，这些灯在互相交流，
Freeman: Now the lights are talking.

169
00:09:31,980 --> 00:09:35,450
当一盏灯亮了，它会引起另一盏灯熄灭，
When one turns on, it signals another to turn off.

170
00:09:35,450 --> 00:09:39,370
当一盏灯熄灭，这个信号又会点亮另一盏灯，以此类推。
When one turns off, it signals another to turn on, and so on.

171
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:42,490
这样，神经元产生了动态的
Together, they create a dynamic symphony

172
00:09:42,490 --> 00:09:44,410
思维和情感，
of thoughts and emotions,

173
00:09:44,410 --> 00:09:47,410
产生了活着的感觉。
leading to the feeling of being alive.

