00:37:48,660 --> 00:37:52,800
包括思维上和身体上。
both mentally and physically.

695
00:37:52,800 --> 00:37:55,240
这是斯巴达比赛，一种障碍赛跑，
So this is the spartan race. It's an obstacle race.

696
00:37:55,240 --> 00:37:57,320
这种比赛是非常艰难的，
This one in particular is a very tough one.

697
00:37:57,320 --> 00:37:58,790
人们都叫它“野兽比赛”。
It's called "the beast."

698
00:37:58,790 --> 00:38:03,810
参赛者要跑上凯灵顿山，大约有14.3公里，25个障碍，
It goes up Mount Killington, about 14.3 miles, 25 obstacles,

699
00:38:03,810 --> 00:38:06,410
需要翻墙，爬绳，
jumping walls, climbing ropes,

700
00:38:06,420 --> 00:38:09,800
泥地匍匐等凡是你能想到的障碍，
under mud ponds, you name it, and, you know,

701
00:38:09,800 --> 00:38:12,650
人们说最杰出的运动员也需要4个小时完成比赛，
they say the elites are gonna do it in four hours.

702
00:38:12,660 --> 00:38:14,000
我们希望能够在8小时内完成，
We're hoping to do it under eight.

703
00:38:14,010 --> 00:38:15,260
我们等会儿再看结果吧。
We'll see what happens.

704
00:38:16,260 --> 00:38:19,430
Marcelo参加这项极端比赛
Marcelo competes in these grueling races

705
00:38:19,430 --> 00:38:20,890
只为一个原因——
for one main reason --

706
00:38:20,900 --> 00:38:23,300
将自己的身体推向极限，
to push his body to the limits

707
00:38:23,300 --> 00:38:25,970
来看他能做到何种程度。
and to find out what he's really made of.

708
00:38:25,970 --> 00:38:30,200
经验告诉他，无论他如何艰苦训练，
It has taught him that, no matter how hard he trains,

709
00:38:30,210 --> 00:38:34,070
也无法达到神的身体状态。
he can never reach the physical levels of a God.

710
00:38:34,080 --> 00:38:35,680
我们的身体极限
Our bodies impose limits

711
00:38:35,680 --> 00:38:38,390
限制了我们能做什么，不能做什么，
on what we can do and what we cannot do.

712
00:38:38,400 --> 00:38:40,950
所以甚至最强的运动员，
So even the most accomplished of athletes,

713
00:38:40,950 --> 00:38:44,350
最完美的身体，也不是彻底的完美。
most perfect body, is never exactly perfect.

714
00:38:44,350 --> 00:38:46,390
Marcelo认为人类
Marcelo believes that humans

715
00:38:46,390 --> 00:38:48,150
不仅有身体极限，
not only have physical limits

716
00:38:48,160 --> 00:38:51,170
阻止我们变成神，
that prevent us from becoming God-like,

717
00:38:51,180 --> 00:38:53,190
我们也有思维极限，
we also have mental limits.

718
00:38:53,190 --> 00:38:56,080
他的证据就在科学之中，
He sees evidence of this in science,

719
00:38:56,080 --> 00:38:58,770
正如物理学家正努力完成
as physicists have been competing

720
00:38:58,770 --> 00:39:01,450
属于他们自己的斯巴达比赛。
in their own cosmic spartan race.

721
00:39:03,720 --> 00:39:05,940
这一切都始于柏拉图，
Gleiser: So it all started with Plato.

722
00:39:05,940 --> 00:39:08,880
柏拉图喜爱几何学，而且他认为
You know, Plato loved geometry, and he thought that,

723
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:11,010
若要理解自然，就要寻找对称，
to understand nature, find symmetry,

724
00:39:11,010 --> 00:39:13,610
寻找最基本的对称，
find the most fundamental symmetry that exists,

725
00:39:13,620 --> 00:39:16,220
这样你就能解开万物的秘密。
and then you unlock the secret of everything.

726
00:39:17,220 --> 00:39:22,250
大多物理学家仍在使用柏拉图对称的观点
Most physicists still use Plato's idea of symmetry

727
00:39:22,260 --> 00:39:26,390
对宇宙万物做出解释。
to try to explain how the universe works.

728
00:39:26,390 --> 00:39:29,310
事物的一半与另一半对应的相同，
When one thing on one side is the same as on the other side,

729
00:39:29,310 --> 00:39:30,560
我们就称之为对称，
we call that a symmetry.

730
00:39:30,560 --> 00:39:33,050
你可以看你的周围，
So you look around yourself,

731
00:39:33,050 --> 00:39:35,970
大自然有如此多的对称，
and the world has all these shapes.

732
00:39:37,670 --> 00:39:41,140
动物，蝴蝶，植物，
Animals, there are butterflies, plants,

733
00:39:41,140 --> 00:39:43,880
这是一种人类的本能
and there is a natural drive of us humans

734
00:39:43,880 --> 00:39:46,650
能够看到万物的对称。
to identify patterns in everything we see.

735
00:39:46,650 --> 00:39:50,220
我们在世界中寻找对称的欲望
Freeman: Our desire to seek symmetry in the world

736
00:39:50,220 --> 00:39:53,490
诱惑物理学家使用同样的道理
has lured physicists into applying this rule

737
00:39:53,490 --> 00:39:56,620
来研究最神秘的谜题——
to one of the greatest mysteries of all --

738
00:39:56,620 --> 00:39:59,290
宇宙是如何出现的。
how the universe began.

739
00:40:00,290 --> 00:40:04,930
许多物理学家认为大爆炸开始之前，
Many physicists believe that just before the big bang,

740
00:40:04,930 --> 00:40:06,830
宇宙就像是一个
the universe was like

741
00:40:06,830 --> 00:40:10,370
有着完美对称性的吊灯，
a perfectly symmetric glass chandelier,

742
00:40:10,370 --> 00:40:13,100
然后突然间...
and suddenly...

743
00:40:13,110 --> 00:40:16,110
[ Whooshing, explosion ]

744
00:40:16,110 --> 00:40:19,990
...整个结构碎成了数亿个碎片。
...the whole fixture shattered into billions of pieces.

745
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:23,050
科学家都在试图将碎片拼回去，
Scientists have been trying to put the pieces back together,

746
00:40:23,050 --> 00:40:25,570
这样就能知道原始结构是什么样的。
to know what the original structure looked like.

747
00:40:25,570 --> 00:40:26,920
嗯。
Hmm.

748
00:40:26,920 --> 00:40:30,150
如果我们能了解万物是如何组合在一起的，
If we can understand how everything fits,

749
00:40:30,160 --> 00:40:33,170
这样人类也许就能在天庭中
then maybe humanity can take God's place

750
00:40:33,180 --> 00:40:35,280
取代神的宝座。
in the celestial throne room.

751
00:40:35,280 --> 00:40:39,160
但Marcelo认为物理学家们试图将事物拼回原状的目标
But Marcelo thinks physicists are trying to put together

752
00:40:39,170 --> 00:40:40,930
是永远无法实现的，
a puzzle that will never fit,

753
00:40:40,930 --> 00:40:43,480
因为当科学家进行实验时，
because when scientists do experiments,

754
00:40:43,490 --> 00:40:46,040
总是无法构成对称。
symmetry often falls apart.

755
00:40:47,810 --> 00:40:50,440
大自然中存在的最有趣的一种粒子
Gleiser: One of the most fascinating particles

756
00:40:50,440 --> 00:40:53,010
就是中微子，
that exists in nature is called the neutrino.

757
00:40:53,010 --> 00:40:54,980
现在我们知道大多数粒子，
Now it turns out that most particles,

758
00:40:54,980 --> 00:40:57,550
就像宇宙中的大多数物体，拥有自旋，
as most things in nature, they spin.

759
00:40:57,850 --> 00:41:00,120
它们旋转运动，
They have a rotational motion.

760
00:41:00,120 --> 00:41:02,340
你会期望中微子
And you would expect the neutrinos,

761
00:41:02,340 --> 00:41:03,670
就像其他粒子一样
like everything else,

762
00:41:03,670 --> 00:41:06,740
会以完美对称的方式顺时针自旋，
could spin clockwise or counterclockwise,

763
00:41:06,740 --> 00:41:08,090
或逆时针自旋，
perfect symmetry.

764
00:41:08,090 --> 00:41:11,180
但结果是自然界中你只能找到
But it turns out that in nature, you only find neutrinos

765
00:41:11,180 --> 00:41:13,230
我们称之为左旋（手征性）的中微子，
that are what we call left-handed.

766
00:41:13,230 --> 00:41:15,270
它们仅以一种特定的方式自旋，
They only spin in a certain way.

767
00:41:15,270 --> 00:41:17,830
大自然似乎不喜欢右旋的中微子，
【上帝是个左撇子？】
Nature does not like right-handed neutrinos.

768
00:41:17,840 --> 00:41:19,950
所以很明显，
So there is clear, right there,

769
00:41:19,950 --> 00:41:22,370
这个最基本的粒子系统
a very fundamental system of particles

770
00:41:22,370 --> 00:41:25,540
说明了自然界并不是完美对称的，
that interact where nature is not perfectly symmetric.

771
00:41:27,280 --> 00:41:29,910
甚至比如我们自己的身体，
So even at the level of our own bodies,

772
00:41:29,910 --> 00:41:32,270
心脏偏左，不是么？
our hearts are on the left, right?

773
00:41:32,270 --> 00:41:34,320
我们的肝脏则在右边，
And our livers are on the right.

774
00:41:34,320 --> 00:41:37,090
然后，实际上，拿我的脸来说，
Then, in fact, if I would get my face,

775
00:41:37,090 --> 00:41:39,590
你认为是对称的，
which you may think is symmetric,

776
00:41:39,590 --> 00:41:43,430
如果我用右侧的脸与左侧的脸对应，
and I would superimpose my left side with my right side,

777
00:41:43,430 --> 00:41:46,610
你就能看到我的脸明显不对称。
I would definitely not look symmetric at all.

778
00:41:46,610 --> 00:41:50,000
Freeman：Marcelo认为自然界的不对称性
Freeman: Marcelo believes the asymmetries of nature

779
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:52,000
说明了我们持有的理论是错误的。
tell us our theories are wrong.

780
00:41:52,000 --> 00:41:57,160
事实上，他怀疑我们会一直错下去，
In fact, he suspects we will always be wrong.

781
00:41:57,160 --> 00:42:00,680
寻找能够解释万物的理论
Finding one theory to explain everything

782
00:42:00,680 --> 00:42:03,650
也许是一场没有终点的比赛。
may be a race with no finish.

783
00:42:04,650 --> 00:42:07,630
Gleiser：我们对自然界的所有知识
Gleiser: Everything that we know about nature

784
00:42:07,630 --> 00:42:09,550
都基于我们如何看待自然界的，
depends on how we see nature.

785
00:42:09,550 --> 00:42:12,220
可我们的工具是有限的，
And it turns out that our tools are limited,

786
00:42:12,220 --> 00:42:14,990
我们从自然界中做出的推论也是有限的，
that what we can infer from nature is limited.

787
00:42:14,990 --> 00:42:16,830
我们不可能知道一切，
We cannot know everything.

788
00:42:16,830 --> 00:42:20,160
我们对于这个世界的理解
It's really about our urge to understand the world

789
00:42:20,160 --> 00:42:23,500
永无尽头，也永远不可能完美，
that is never final and never perfect.

790
00:42:23,500 --> 00:42:26,520
而总有一些未知，
This notion that there is always something else,

791
00:42:26,520 --> 00:42:30,390
一些阻碍我们认知事物的不平衡，
that there is always a imbalance in the way we perceive things,

792
00:42:30,390 --> 00:42:32,770
才造就了现在的人类。
is what makes us human.

793
00:42:32,780 --> 00:42:37,480
人类正在努力做到全知全能，
The human drive to become all-powerful and all-knowing

794
00:42:37,480 --> 00:42:40,200
但这看起来是永无止境的。
seems unstoppable.

795
00:42:40,200 --> 00:42:43,740
科学给了我们惊人的力量，
Science has given us tremendous power,

796
00:42:43,740 --> 00:42:47,710
而我们也有或许永远无法克服的局限，
but we have limitations that we may never overcome.

797
00:42:47,710 --> 00:42:51,460
但这也许是一个礼物，
But maybe our fallibilities are a gift.

798
00:42:51,460 --> 00:42:53,460
毕竟，
After all,

799
00:42:53,460 --> 00:42:56,050
正是这种局限使我们不断前进，
they are what keep us striving to achieve

800
00:42:56,050 --> 00:42:57,570
不断完成看似不可能的事情。
what seems impossible.

